\fBgetComputedStyle(selector, msg)\fR
Retrieves the computed styles for a given element.
.br
// Using CSS selector const style = getComputedStyle('.my\-element', 'Custom success message');
.br
// Using Element object const el = document.querySelector('.my\-element'); const style = getComputedStyle(el);
\fBParameters:\fR
.br
\fIselector\fR (string \\| Element; required) The CSS selector or the Element object for which to get the computed styles.
.br
\fImsg\fR (string; optional) An optional message to display when the operation is successful. Default message will be generated based on the type of selector.
\fBReturns:\fR
.br
\fICSSStyleDeclaration\fR The computed styles of the element.
